<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-android36.0</TargetFramework>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion>24</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.App.Android</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.App.Android</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Suppressed Build Warnings — Documentation
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    These four codes are raised by this project and by nothing else in the repository, so
    they are suppressed here rather than in the root Directory.Build.props. Suppressing them
    repo-wide would silence the same codes in hand-written application code — a CS8601 newly
    introduced in Broiler.Writer.Core would disappear behind a suppression that exists for
    .NET for Android binding signatures.

    Measured 2026-09-02, against a clean Rebuild of all five solutions with every NoWarn
    lifted: 4x CS8604, 2x CS8601, 2x CS8603 and 16x CA1416, all in this project, and none of
    the four raised anywhere else.

    ── Nullable Reference Type Warnings ──────────────────────────────
    CS8601 : Possible null reference assignment
    CS8603 : Possible null reference return
    CS8604 : Possible null reference argument

    Reason  : .NET for Android binding signatures that are annotated non-nullable but are
              documented to accept null (Canvas.DrawColor's PorterDuff.Mode,
              Bitmap.CreateBitmap's Bitmap.Config).
    Future  : Revisit when the Android bindings tighten their nullability annotations.

    ── Platform Compatibility ────────────────────────────────────────
    CA1416 : Call site reachable on all platforms but API is version-gated

    Reason  : This project targets a minimum SDK of 24 and calls WindowInsets.GetInsets (30),
              Insets members (29) and LockHardwareCanvas (26) behind `Build.VERSION.SdkInt`
              checks the analyzer does not recognise as guards. The legacy branches already
              carry targeted `#pragma warning disable CS0618, CA1422`, so the runtime gating
              is real.
    Future  : No action expected; the guard is correct and the analyzer is imprecise.

    The nullable warnings the component submodules raise (CS8602, CS8618, CS8625) stay in the
    root Directory.Build.props, because they are not this project's and are not this
    project's to describe.
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS8601;CS8603;CS8604;CA1416</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Graphics\src\Broiler.Graphics\Broiler.Graphics.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Input\src\Broiler.Input.Android\Broiler.Input.Android.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Input\src\Broiler.Input.Keyboard.Android\Broiler.Input.Keyboard.Android.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Input\src\Broiler.Input.Pen.Android\Broiler.Input.Pen.Android.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Input\src\Broiler.Input.Text.Android\Broiler.Input.Text.Android.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.Input\src\Broiler.Input.Touch.Android\Broiler.Input.Touch.Android.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Broiler.UI\src\Foundation\Broiler.UI\Broiler.UI.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
